{
	x: 7.0d,
	y: 18.0d,
	text: [
		"These bad boys can store 10 MHE of power (a lot) and they are rather easy to set up.",
		"",
		"You put one of these adjacent to a cable and, by default, they will regulate all of the current charge in the grid to them, if any surpluss is present they will store it and if it's needed it will share it .",
		"",
		"Right click a battery to configure it. There are three ways the battery can store power: ",
		"",
		"- Green \"<->\"  (which is the default) which regulates the current surpluss between all batteries. ",
		"- Orange \"^\" which will drain the batterie's energy into the power grid it's connected to",
		"- Blue \"v\" which will store as much energy as possible from the grid (without sharing any).",
		"- Gray \"X\" the battery is disabled and doesn't interact with the grid, storing it's current power.",
		"",
		"To change the behavior press the buttons on the menu, there are two, to the left and right.",
		"",
		"The left configuration button will only work if the battery is not powered by redstone.",
		"The right configuration button will only work if the battery is powered by redstone.",
		"",
		"You may also change the priority of the battery and charge or discharge individual battery cells."
	],
